8. Lists

Definition
A mutable collection used to store multiple values.
skills = ["Python", "Java", "SQL"]


Access
skills[0]


Add
skills.append("React")


Remove
skills.remove("Java")


Length
len(skills)


Loop
for skill in skills:
    print(skill)


Interview Question
List vs Tuple?
List is mutable.
Tuple is immutable.

9. Tuples

Definition
Immutable collection.
skills = ("Python", "Java")


Access
skills[0]


Interview Question
Why use Tuple?
Use when data should not change.

10. Sets

Definition
Stores unique values.
skills = {"Python", "Java", "Python"}

Result:
{"Python", "Java"}


Add
skills.add("React")


Remove
skills.remove("Java")


Interview Question
Why use Set?
To remove duplicates.
Industry Term:
Deduplication


11. Dictionaries

Definition
Stores data as key-value pairs.
